   ],
   "definition_quote": "We consider a stochastic contextual bandits problem with $K$ arms... In contextual USS, the arms are assumed to be ordered and form a cascade. When the learner selects an arm $i \\in [K]$, the feedback from all arms till arm $i$ in the cascade are observed. The expected loss of playing the arm $i$ for a given context $\\xt$ is denoted as $\\gamma_i(\\xt) \\doteq \\Prob{\\Yti \\neq \\Yt|X=\\xt}$... The total expected loss incurred by playing arm $i$ for context $\\xt$ is defined as $\\gamma_i(\\xt)+\\lambda_iC_i$"
